The load address layout:

  kernel_addr_r       0x80200000  (16MB)
  kernel_comp_addr_r  0x81200000  (16MB)
  fdt_addr_r          0x82200000
  scriptaddr          0x82300000
  pxefile_addr_r      0x82400000
  ramdisk_addr_r      0x82500000

packs everything into the first ~37MB of the 64MB DRAM, which looks fine
arithmetically, but ramdisk_addr_r at 0x82500000 leaves only ~27MB for the
ramdisk/initrd before hitting the end of DRAM (0x80000000+0x4000000=
0x84000000). Given CONFIG_SYS_SDRAM_BASE here is presumably 0x80000000,
can you confirm the 64MB figure accounts for the full board (both milkv_duo
and milkv_duo_256m use this same .env, per the series), not just the 256M
variant?

Also kernel_comp_size=0x1000000 (16MB) for the compressed kernel staging
area - is this validated against the largest kernel image you've tested, or
just a conservative round number carried over from other boards' envs?

Patches 2/3 and 3/3 (enabling BOOTSTD_DEFAULTS and reducing
CONFIG_STACK_SIZE to 1MB) weren't included in this file snippet I reviewed -
please confirm reducing the stack size doesn't regress any SPL/boot path
given the DRAM is only 64MB total here.
